2026-10-11T19:00:23.2812336Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2821833Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2911589Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2919725Z [0m
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2920237Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2920759Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2921157Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2921362Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2921760Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2921961Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2922167Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2922477Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2922609Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2922950Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2923385Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2923893Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2924305Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2924680Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2924953Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2925261Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2925518Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2925808Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2925914Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2926002Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2926125Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2926413Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2926800Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2931507Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2931604Z I will:
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2931737Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2931939Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2932449Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2933104Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2933492Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2933865Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2934093Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2934426Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T19:00:23.2934712Z    /root
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3918462Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3919115Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3928108Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3928524Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3928789Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3930658Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3931032Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3946887Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3947534Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3956751Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3957250Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3957757Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3957981Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3958197Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3958462Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3958767Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3959309Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3959559Z 
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3959698Z If you would like to
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3960097Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-11T19:00:23.3960388Z 
